# Test kernel: the scalar printer's branch over a fix-up (cpp.branch; milestone1.md, "Emission").
# Every output is a select on m1, and every first arm a select on m2: the branch tests m1 & m2,
# after s, m1 and m2. The arms it then returns are a value (s), the literal zero and an input (a).
# The fix-up needs d and q, which nothing before the branch needs, and s, which it shares. A NaN a
# makes m1 false, a NaN b makes m2 false, independently. Its claim is not judged.
kernel:   ops_branch
input:    a
input:    b
output:   x = x0 x1
output:   y
value:    a
ensures:  represents x
status:   unverified
domain:   extended
ieee_status: unverified
cone_exempt: a test of the scalar printer's branch, not of a computation

s  = add(a, b)
m1 = eq(a, a)
m2 = eq(b, b)
d  = sub(a, b)
q  = times_inf(d)
h  = select(m2, s, q)
k  = select(m2, 0, d)
l  = select(m2, a, b)
x0 = select(m1, h, q)
x1 = select(m1, k, d)
y  = select(m1, l, s)
